+ {"status": "in_progress", "id": "AUG-133", "title": "Published XSD is decorative: the validator never loads it and the schema cannot express the <test> surface", "detail": {"fingerprint": "5f0f8971b0aeaaa15741faf957ce3c8dd494a3cb97bb347c5cc9ce96c55c1bf9"}, "priority": "P1", "source": null, "reasoning": "Measured 2026-11-05 at HEAD 10ef0d7. specs/schema/auger-spec-1.0.xsd is never loaded by auger.py: 'grep -rn \"xsd|XMLSchema|lxml\" auger.py' returns comments only (7699, 8469). Validation is hand-written in _spec_validate_blocks (auger.py:8022), and the only schema-aware test (tests/test_xml_specs.py:173 test_schema_matches_the_validator) compares pattern/enUM STRINGS, so a schema the processor would reject still passes. The XSD declares section/requirement/acceptance/verification but has no <test> element and none of the attributes the code requires on one (runner, selector, path, migration, fixture, assertions, type). Consequence: the normative grammar and the enforced grammar are different languages, and an editor validating a real AUG-123 obligation against the shipped XSD flags it invalid. The schema is normative by the PRD's own wording, so today the normative half is a comment while the hand-written half decides.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: the validator loads specs/schema/auger-spec-1.0.xsd with a real XML Schema processor and a fixture that violates the XSD fails validation with a typed error (a fixture that is well-formed and code-acceptable but schema-invalid must be refused) - proven by a test that runs the shipped schema against the shipped fixtures.\nPASS: every attribute the code reads on every block kind is expressible in the schema - a test enumerates the attribute names auger.py requires (including runner, selector, path, migration, fixture, assertions, type, method) and asserts each is declared in the XSD, so the two cannot drift again.\nPASS: the <test> element is declared in the XSD, or the schema is restru