++ {"status": "pending", "id": "AUG-160", "title": "[P2] GitReins tier1 evidence attaches the NEWEST OLD guard log to every step, so a PASS verdict cites an artifact that says FAIL", "detail": {"fingerprint": "ec3e91233da14dc64f8d1a5cfaf60b1e69887c6cd65ea949e9aadf53c2d6c7c1"}, "priority": "P2", "source": null, "reasoning": "MEASURED 2026-11-08 on verdict cca14d17 (task AUG-158-159-R1, commit 7d4fd96, pass_class=judged, 7/7 items PASS). All three tier1 steps carry data.guard_log=/home/kara/auger/.gitreins/logs/guard-20261105T170854.274025Z.log. That file's header reads run_utc 2026-11-05T17:08:54Z (2.6 days before the verdict's evaluated_at 2026-11-08T07:26:13Z), its own overall line reads 'FAIL (DEGRADED — skipped checks)', and it contains zero ruff output (grep -c ruff -> 0). The newest log in .gitreins/logs/ is still the Nov-5 file, so the task-complete path wrote none; engine/guard_manager.py:1259 newest_guard_log() supplies whatever exists. Net effect: a green verdict's own evidence pointer contradicts it, an auditor cannot tell which run produced the lint/secrets/tests lines, and the same fallback would happily attach an OLD PASS log to a current FAIL step.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: a fresh verdict's tier1 steps no longer cite a guard log from another run — for every step in `stages.tier1.steps`, `data.guard_log` either is absent or names a file whose `run_utc:` header is within 30 minutes of the verdict's `evaluated_at`. Probe: `cd /home/kara/auger && python3 -c \"import json,pathlib,datetime as dt;d=json.load(open('.gitreins/history/<DATE>/<RUN>/verdict.json'));ev=dt.datetime.fromisoformat(d['evaluated_at']);[print(s['id'], (p:=s['data'].get('guard_log')), (lambda t:(abs((ev-t).total_seconds())<1800 if t else 'absent'))(dt.datetime.fromisoformat([l for l in open(p) if l.startswith('run_utc:')][0].split(':',1)[1].strip().replace('Z','')) ) if p else 'absent') for s in d['stages']['tier1']['steps']]\"` -> every step print