+++ {"id":"AUG-118","status":"in_progress","priority":"P1","complexity":5,"title":"XML spec source + targeted cross-file assembly: sections, attributes, references and verification","reasoning":"Owner request: Auger needs XML-authoritative specifications where stable IDs, kinds, applicability, versions, and verification methods are attributes; a selector can assemble the relevant sections across files without loading whole documents. Current `export --profile nasa` is Markdown only and does not implement XML selection/transclusion. Keep the feature additive and preserve existing Markdown export. Use the ch:trace discipline from ~/.hermes/skills/coding-hermes-traceability/SKILL.md and align the spec with the repo's docs/DESIGN.md; include explicit cross-file references and auditable evidence.","acceptance_criteria":"1. A versioned XML schema defines stable requirement/block IDs and attributes for kind, applies-to, status/version, and verification method.\n2. A CLI can select by ID and attributes and assemble selected blocks from at least two XML files in deterministic order, preserving source IDs and citations.\n3. Refusal tests cover unresolved references, duplicate IDs, cycles, unsupported schema versions, and invalid verification metadata; no partial document is emitted on failure.\n4. A golden test proves default Markdown export remains unchanged and XML selection emits only the requested blocks plus their explicit dependencies.\n5. The new spec records rationale, alternatives, verification, and `ch:trace row=AUG-118 ` with a repository-relative spec anchor and tests/evidence; CI/guard runs the new tests.","depends_on":[],"files_changed":[],"foreman_note":"PRD: docs/prd/xml-spec-graph.md\n\nMEASURED BUILT - DO NOT RE-IMPLEMENT. Row moved pending -> in_progress on measured evidence (2026-11-05, HEAD 10ef0d7). Landing commit ea819d9 'feat(spec): XML spec source + targeted cross-file assembly (AUG-118)'. Measured on this tree: (1) 'auger spec validate tests/fixtures