+++ {"id":"AUG-119","status":"in_progress","priority":"P1","complexity":4,"title":"Approved Auger plan ↔ boardctl task lifecycle integration","reasoning":"Auger currently has no boardctl-backed task create/update lifecycle. Existing Auger planning contract requires drafts not to write the canonical board or dispatch work until a human approves a specific plan version; boardctl is the canonical writer and the existing scheduler remains dispatch authority. This row links the request to that approval boundary and ch:trace doctrine.","acceptance_criteria":"1. Auger can produce a versioned draft plan with task IDs, acceptance criteria, dependencies, source spec anchors, and expected verification evidence.\n2. No board mutation occurs before explicit approval bound to the plan version/digest; rejected or stale approvals refuse export.\n3. After approval, Auger invokes the supported boardctl CLI/API (no parallel board store) to create/update canonical board rows and reads them back to verify exact IDs and criteria.\n4. Board status/commit/verdict evidence can be reconciled into Auger without Auger dispatching or overwriting canonical board state.\n5. Tests prove idempotent export, partial-failure recovery, and that unapproved drafts leave tasks.jsonl/events.jsonl byte-identical.\n6. Ch:trace includes row/spec/test/evidence/witness and explicit none:<reason> values for absent fields; commits and verdicts are bound as required by the traceability skill.","depends_on":[],"files_changed":[],"foreman_note":"PRD: docs/prd/xml-spec-graph.md\n\nZERO CODE - GENUINELY UNSTARTED (measured 2026-11-05, HEAD 10ef0d7). 'grep -c boardctl auger.py' -> 0 in an 8983-line module; 'grep -n \"tasks.jsonl|events.jsonl\" auger.py' -> no matches. There is no plan object, no plan digest, no approval ledger, no boardctl client, no read-back comparator, and no 'approved plan' concept in the spec schema. Nothing about this row is built: it is the largest single missing piece of the PRD (R9) and a worker starts from zero. Do not look for partial work under a different name - the only board-related code in the repo is tests/ and docs/, never auger.py.\n\nSG8 DISPATCHED 2026-11-06 from base 53f09d3 (goal auger-xml-hardening). Brief /home/kara/.hermes/goals/auger-xml-hardening-SG8-brief.txt. Builds ON the SG7 boardctl seam (do not rebuild it): single-task export at auger.py ~L9279 (_boardctl ~L9201, _board_readback ~L9217, _approved_digest ~L9003). Scope = versioned draft PLAN + digest-bound approval + multi-row idempotent export + partial-failure record + board status/commit/verdict reconciliation into Auger; proof file tests/test_plan_approval.py (absent at base, measured).\n\nSG8 VERIFIED AND MERGED 2026-11-06 (driver tick). Commit 369807b on main (ff-merge from wt/auger-xml-hardening; origin parity 0/0). Code: spec plan-draft/plan-approve/plan-export/plan-reconcile, versioned plan with digest-bound approval ledger, multi-row boardctl create/update/show with field-by-field readback, idempotent re-export (unchanged, 0 bytes), partial-failure recovery record + resume, read-only reconciliation with none:<reason> for absent evidence. Proof: tests/test_plan_approval.py (11 tests) in the gate pytest arm. Verified by the driver, not trusted from the worker: falsifiers.sh 6/6 reproduced (0 failures), 41 focused tests green, gate PASS rc 0 on the worktree tree (585 passed/2 skipped/914.74s) AND on merged main (585 passed/2 skipped/889.77s). Disclosed limits: single commit for both rows (module+proof coupling), boardctl update cannot rewrite scope (refuses board-row-conflict rather than overwriting canonical state). STATUS LEFT in_progress: no GitReins verdict artifact, so no evidence-run-id and no close.","worker_status":"done","commit_hash":"369807b5ccc5bdaf0a05a6a1f6193693999eb901","completed_at":null,"guard_result":null,"ci_result":null,"detail":{"fingerprint":"7979bfc13cecf2907d491bd371227cde9ce0d221c827e2d021ea36a9c2aac5e3"},"lines_added":0,"lines_removed":0,"attempt