+++-{"id":"AUG-120","status":"in_progress","priority":"P1","complexity":5,"title":"Auger staged-change spec alignment and ch:trace check interface for GitReins","reasoning":"Provide GitReins a reusable Auger checker rather than implementing a second evaluator. The check must explain which spec blocks relate to a staged diff, whether the change and comments/docs match their intended section, and which required ch:trace links are missing. Use the ch:trace skill and public traceability doctrine; reports must cite evidence rather than inventing rationale or claiming semantic certainty.","acceptance_criteria":"1. A documented, machine-readable Auger CLI/API accepts a staged diff plus repository/spec root and returns referenced spec IDs/blocks, trace-link findings, and evidence locations.\n2. It checks changed code/comments/docs against the selected spec sections and reports missing, misplaced, or contradictory spec/trace annotations with a concrete why and source citation.\n3. It validates the ch:trace marker contract (row mandatory; absent values explicit; evidence not another row; verdict bound to commit) using the loaded traceability doctrine.\n4. No changes are written to source, specs, or boards; result is deterministic JSON with pass/warn/fail and findings.\n5. Fixture tests cover aligned change, missing trace, wrong spec section, contradictory comment, and no-related-spec cases; the latter is reported as unscoped, not an automatic pass.\n6. Full acceptance criteria and a ch:trace row are committed with this task.","depends_on":["AUG-118"],"files_changed":[],"foreman_note":"PRD: docs/prd/xml-spec-graph.md\n\nZERO CODE - GENUINELY UNSTARTED (measured 2026-11-05, HEAD 10ef0d7). 'grep -c \"diff-stdin|protocol-version|repo-root\" auger.py' -> 0; 'grep -n \"staged|--diff\" auger.py' -> no matches. No verb accepts a diff, so there is no staged-diff spec-alignment checker and no ch:trace contract validator: the 3 'ch:trace' occurrences in auger.py are prose comments (lines 95, 7708, 7709), not a parser. This row is the Auger half of the seam GitReins already calls (GR-154 is status: complete and invokes --repo-root/--spec-root/--protocol-version/--diff-stdin); a fix must satisfy the caller's argv, which is tracked as its own P1 row. Build from zero; there is nothing to extend.\n\nSG5 dispatched 2026-11-05T18:23Z with AUG-135 (same worker/pid 3354505, same brief). Staged-diff spec alignment + ch:trace contract validation, deterministic JSON (pass|warn|fail), no writes to source/specs/boards, five fixture cases incl. no-related-spec=unscoped. Measured zero code at d2f9a50 (no verb accepts a diff).\n\nSG5 VERIFIED AND MERGED (driver, 2026-11-05), same wave as AUG-135: main e1adcd3 (origin/main parity 0/0), gated tree 3fefd8e7 == merged tree.\nAC1: the staged-diff checker is documented and machine-readable - `auger spec align`/`auger spec check --diff-stdin` take --repo-root/--spec-root/--protocol-version and emit referenced ids/blocks, trace findings and evidence locations as one JSON line (driver transcript evidence/auger-SG5/09-driver-verification.txt; payload keys referenced.paths/referenced.blocks/referenced.unresolved + findings[].evidence).\nAC2: findings carry a concrete why and a source citation - measured `{\"code\":\"trace-spec-unresolved\",\"evidence\":\"src_change.py:4\",\"severity\":\"fail\",\"why\":\"spec=AUG-SPEC-1 does not resolve: ...\"}`, and contradictory/superseded sections are separate codes (test_a_contradictory_comment_citing_a_superseded_section_fails, test_a_wrong_spec_section_is_reported).\nAC3: the ch:trace contract is validated with DISTINCT findings per violation class - test_the_ch_trace_contract_violations_are_distinct_findings.\nAC4: read-only and deterministic - driver probe: 0 status changes in the repo under test, 0 dirty lines in the worktree; test_the_checker_writes_nothing_and_is_deterministic; status is pass|warn|fail with scope scoped|unscoped|empty.\nAC5: five fixture cases present - aligned (test_an_aligned_change_passes_with_resolved_spec_ids), missing trace (test_a_missing_trace_is_a_named_failure), wrong section (test_a_wrong_spec_section_is_reported), contradictory (test_a_contradictory_comment_citing_a_superseded_section_fails), no-related-spec reported UNSCOPED not pass (test_a_change_with_no_related_spec_is_unscoped_not_pass).\nAC6: the ch:trace marker is committed in tests/test_spec_alignment_check.py's header (row=AUG-135,AUG-120 spec=docs/prd/xml-spec-graph.md#R11); verdict=none:pending-judge is explicit, not invented.\nGATE: rc 0 on the worktree tree and rc 0 on merged main (507 passed / 2 skipped, 859.62s / 856.63s). GUARD = SKIP (worker used core.hooksPath=/dev/null, disclosed) - gate is the substitute.\nROW STAYS in_progress: semantic contradiction detection is structural only (documented as out of scope, AUG-142 rides this finding channel), and no commit-bound GitReins verdict exists for e1adcd3.\n\nCI/COMMIT REBIND (driver, 2026-11-05): commit_hash -> e1adcd3, the merged tip that CARRIES the checker (c0e948f + 266d378 are its parents; a pre-merge commit has no CI run of its own because it landed inside this push). ci=GREEN from run 42147268622 conclusion=success headSha=e1adcd33023fa4e8ed3a7c13cf88202aebd3a282, matched by prefix from `gh run list --limit 8 --json status,conclusion,name,headSha`. guard_result stays SKIP: no GitReins Tier-1/Tier-2 verdict exists for this tree - and note that a judge here re-runs `bash tests/gate.sh` (tier1 test_command, test_mode full) with a 90m tier-2 cap, so the verdict run is its own scheduled action, not a tail-end step of the merge.","worker_status":"complete","commit_hash":"e1adcd3","completed_at":null,"guard_result":"SKIP","ci_result":"GREEN","detail":{"fingerprint":"fc2a00c3ae29d1218c67215be9f4c7be3fde84bed873d06c1d2439eefcd772c7"},"lines_added":0,"lines_removed":0,"attempts":0,"blocked_reason":null,"capability_tags":["gitreins","spec-alignment","ch-trace","pre-commit","verification"],"created_at":"