++++ {"status": "in_progress", "id": "AUG-136", "title": "No authored spec corpus exists: specs/ holds only the XSD, so nothing in the repo uses the machinery it ships", "detail": {"fingerprint": "a334a5ca2906d2a1e24927d660d717049436147c0d450ed0532b3ff4e0314f98"}, "priority": "P2", "source": null, "reasoning": "Measured 2026-11-05 at HEAD 10ef0d7: 'find specs -name \"*.xml\"' -> 0 files; specs/ contains exactly specs/schema/auger-spec-1.0.xsd. 'auger spec validate specs' -> 'spec error (empty-corpus)', rc 2. Every XML document in the repository is a test fixture under tests/fixtures/xml/ (3 valid corpus files, 8 negative fixture directories, 1 verification corpus). The PRD's first requirement is that XML is the authoritative source and Markdown/HTML are generated views; with no authored document that claim is exercised only against synthetic fixtures, and the Markdown view is a golden file nobody reads. Nothing in the repo would notice if the renderer produced a stale or wrong view of a real document.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: at least one real authored .xml spec document lives under specs/ (not under tests/) and covers an actual Auger surface - its requirement/acceptance/verification blocks name real auger.py verbs and real tests in this repository, not fixture names.\nPASS: CI validates that corpus on every run ('auger spec validate specs' with rc 0 is an arm in tests/gate.sh or the workflow, so an empty or broken corpus fails the build instead of passing silently).\nPASS: the authored corpus is the source for a generated Markdown view committed to docs/, and a test regenerates that view from the XML and asserts byte equality, so the view cannot drift from its source.", "complexity": 2, "created_at": "2026-11-05T12:59:24.951137+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-06T09:37:19.163444+00:00", "foreman_note": "2026-11-05 wave: merged on main 6b0d190 (spec-a 7bb5565/c6b24b3/c84f617, spec-b 4b27c83/8375d78/35267f6, corpus 20731e8); ful