+++++ {"status": "complete", "id": "AUG-157", "evidence_run_id": "46f7677f", "title": "Shipped example corpus claims it validates outside any repository; at HEAD it refuses unresolvable-repo-root without --repo-root", "detail": {"fingerprint": "d81aa6f62664d92a5d6b18a358fef338698b08d33257f329e0ad5cd7ef99041e", "evidence": [{"run_id":"b15d6edc","ts":"2026-11-08T02:06:56.102815+00:00"},{"run_id":"46f7677f","ts":"2026-11-08T19:57:13.685909+00:00"}]}, "priority": "P2", "source": null, "reasoning": "MEASURED 2026-11-07 at main f852b86 during the goal-check tick. examples/xml/minimal.xml lines 9-10 (shipped byte-identical into the wheel at share/auger/specs/examples/minimal.xml — diff rc 0 against the installed copy) states: 'Deliberately obligation-free: no type=test block, so the corpus names no repository-relative test path and validates outside any repository'. That published claim is false at HEAD: from a non-git directory, 'auger.py spec validate <dir holding minimal.xml>' -> rc 2 'spec error (invalid-spec-graph): unresolvable-repo-root: <dir> is not inside a git work tree and no --repo-root was given', and 'spec check' refuses with the identical diagnostic (so this is not the old two-validator split). Cause: _spec_repository_root() (auger.py:13087) is resolved EAGERLY by validate_xml_specs for every corpus, before any obligation is read, so a corpus that declares no path/migration/fixture at all still cannot be graded without a repository. The docs disagree with themselves: docs/XML-SPEC-SCHEMA.md:47 says the example gives 'a fresh install ... something real to validate without a git checkout', but the command it prints two lines later passes --repo-root \"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\", and tests/test_packaging_wheel.py:307-330 replays it against a throwaway 'git init'. Goal A9 passes as tested (fresh venv + documented command + rc 0), so this row is the residual: a user-facing promise printed inside the artifact that nothing enforces. Two acceptable resolutio